            <ArticleTitle>Mayer-Rokitansky-Kuster-Hauser syndrome associated with rectovestibular fistula.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>70-73</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4274/tjod.94809</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A female neonate with two openings in the introitus and an absent anal opening at the anal site presents a diagnostic challenge. Mayer-Rokitansky-Kuster-Hauser (MRKH) syndrome associated with rectovestibular fistula, though rare, should be kept in mind as a differential diagnosis of this presentation. We present such a case in a one-year-old female child with MRKH syndrome and rectovestibular fistula.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
